'''
project/
├── main.py                  ← Entry point; currently only loads RoadData.json.
│                               Needs to: create SimPy env, load network.pkl,
│                               instantiate all components, start the simulation.
│
├── config.py                ← All static parameters, organized by section.
│                               Sections: SIMULATION, ROAD_NETWORK, TRAFFIC_MODEL,
│                               CAR, CAR_GENERATOR, SHUTTLE_BUS, TICKET_SCAN,
│                               VISITOR, VISITOR_GENERATOR. No runtime objects.
│
├── visualisation.py         ← Empty. Will read output CSVs/JSONs and
│                               produce all figures and maps.
│
├── functions/
│   ├── TrafficFlowModel.py  ← Core traffic model. Contains:
│   │                            - TrafficDensityMap: stores per-edge density,
│   │                              rho_max, u_max_ms, length, background density.
│   │                            - greenshields_speed(): u = u_max*(1 - rho/rho_max)
│   │                            - edge_travel_time(): travel time from density map
│   │                            - shortest_path(): Dijkstra weighted by travel time
│   │                            - init_from_graph(): populates map from OSMnx graph
│   │                            - background_density_update(): SimPy process that
│   │                              updates background density hourly with interpolation
│   │
│   ├── TVisitorGenerator.py ← Samples N arrival times from gamma distribution,
│   │                           sorts them, computes inter-arrival gaps, and spawns
│   │                           one TVisitor per gap via SimPy timeouts.
│   │
│   ├── TVisitor.py          ← Individual visitor entity. Picks transport mode,
│   │                           assigns start node (car) or station (bus), joins
│   │                           the appropriate queue, passivates/reactivates
│   │                           through each journey phase, walks to ticket scan.
│   │
│   ├── TCarGenerator.py     ← Spawns one manage_node() process per start node.
│   │                           Each loop creates a new TCar and waits for its
│   │                           departed_event before creating the next one —
│   │                           ensuring exactly one car waits at each node at all times.
│   │
│   ├── TCar.py              ← Car entity. Boards visitors up to capacity or
│   │                           max_wait_time (AnyOf pattern), signals departed_event,
│   │                           computes shortest path, drives segment-by-segment
│   │                           updating density before/after each yield, then
│   │                           requests a parking lot slot.
│   │
│   ├── TShuttleBus.py       ← Runs N bus processes over a shared boarding queue.
│   │                           Each bus: boards passengers up to capacity or timeout,
│   │                           drives to festival via road network (density-aware),
│   │                           alights passengers (reactivating each), drives back
│   │                           empty, repeats.
│   │
│   └── TTicketScan.py       ← Runs NumScanLanes scanner processes over a shared
│                               FIFO queue. Each scanner: gets next visitor, waits
│                               scan time, reactivates visitor (journey complete).
│
├── Prepare_network.py       ← One-time script. Loads network.osm via OSMnx,
│                               computes rho_max = (length/Car_Spacing)*lanes and
│                               u_max_ms from OSM maxspeed tags, saves result as
│                               network.pkl.
│
├── RoadData_converter.py    ← One-time script. Converts the raw RoadData.json
│                               (Overpass API format) into a valid OSM XML file
│                               that OSMnx can load.
│
├── roaddata_prep.py         ← One-time script. Reads Excel loop detector data,
│                               extracts average Saturday flows per detector per hour,
│                               saves as flow_2_3_avg.csv for use in
│                               background_density_update().
│
└── find_nodes.py            ← One-time utility. Uses ox.nearest_nodes() to map
                                GPS coordinates to OSMnx node IDs for entry points,
                                bus stop, and parking lot.
'''


